# spr1_check: checker of Sporos bytecode — independent second check of stage 1 (Root A is bootstrap/roots/sporos/sporos-stage1.hex).
#
# What it does: reads a Sporos bytecode file (formal/Sporos/Bytecode.lean) from
# standard input and checks it as Sporos.decode and Sporos.checkProg
# (formal/Sporos/Check.lean) do, three times, on three copies of the input.
#
# Exit status: 0 when the file decodes and passes the checker; 5 when it is
# malformed or ill-typed; 6 when memory is refused or a stack height reaches
# 2^64; 3 when the three passes all disagree. Every non-zero status is at
# Hamming distance 2 or more from 0.
#
# Structure (addresses are 0x400000 + file offset):
#   start   (0x403eaf)  mmap a 64 KiB buffer, read all of stdin, doubling it
#                        with mremap; triplicate the input into two more
#                        mappings; descriptors (base, N) at 0x600000,
#                        0x601000, 0x602000; rax = rbx = rcx = REJECT.
#   tripled (0x400290)  pass 1 (result in rax), pass 2 (rbx), pass 3 (rcx).
#                        Each pass reads only its own copy and descriptor, makes
#                        no store, call, push or syscall, and writes only its
#                        result register: ACCEPT 0x5acce970a55a3c96, REJECT
#                        0xdeadbeef11110001 or OVERFLOW 0xbad0f1e33c3c3a5.
#   vote    (0x40296c)  the 38-byte voter of Bootstrap/TMRVoter.lean, with its
#                        park (eb fe) replaced by eb 0c, a jump to the guard.
#   guard   (0x402992)  exit(0) only when rax - ACCEPT and rbx - ACCEPT are both
#                        zero, tested by two conditional branches; the exit
#                        status is computed from the two differences.
#
# The bytes 0f 85 (jne rel32, one bit from syscall 0f 05) never occur, and
# 0f 05 occurs only at the syscalls.
#
# Total 16402 bytes.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- ELF header
7f 45 4c 46                     # 000  e_ident: magic 0x7f E L F
02                              # 004  ELFCLASS64
01                              # 005  little endian
01                              # 006  EI_VERSION = 1
00                              # 007  System V
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00         # 008  padding
02 00                           # 010  e_type = ET_EXEC
3e 00                           # 012  e_machine = EM_X86_64
01 00 00 00                     # 014  e_version = 1
af 3e 40 00 00 00 00 00         # 018  e_entry
40 00 00 00 00 00 00 00         # 020  e_phoff = 0x40
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00         # 028  e_shoff = 0
00 00 00 00                     # 030  e_flags = 0
40 00                           # 034  e_ehsize = 64
38 00                           # 036  e_phentsize = 56
02 00                           # 038  e_phnum = 2
00 00                           # 03a  e_shentsize = 0
00 00                           # 03c  e_shnum = 0
00 00                           # 03e  e_shstrndx = 0

# ----------------------------------------------------------- program headers
01 00 00 00                     # 040  PT_LOAD (code)
05 00 00 00                     # 044  PF_R | PF_X
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00         # 048  p_offset = 0
00 00 40 00 00 00 00 00         # 050  p_vaddr = 0x400000
00 00 40 00 00 00 00 00         # 058  p_paddr
12 40 00 00 00 00 00 00         # 060  p_filesz = whole file
12 40 00 00 00 00 00 00         # 068  p_memsz
00 10 00 00 00 00 00 00         # 070  p_align = 0x1000
01 00 00 00                     # 078  PT_LOAD (descriptors)
06 00 00 00                     # 07c  PF_R | PF_W
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00         # 080  p_offset = 0
00 00 60 00 00 00 00 00         # 088  p_vaddr = 0x600000
00 00 60 00 00 00 00 00         # 090  p_paddr
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00         # 098  p_filesz = 0
00 30 00 00 00 00 00 00         # 0a0  p_memsz = 0x3000 (three pages)
00 10 00 00 00 00 00 00         # 0a8  p_align = 0x1000

